exports[`initBehaviorDir.integration given: [case1] guard level is light (default) when: [t0] initBehaviorDir is called without guard arg then: vision, criteria, and blueprint stones point the writer at the wisher-how rule 1`] = `
{
  "blueprint": "propose a blueprint for how we will implement the wish
- in .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/0.wish.md
- with .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/3.2.distill.domain.*.yield.md (if declared)
- with .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/3.2.distill.repros.experience.*.yield.md (if declared)

.why = blueprint the code changes needed to deliver the product.
- the product is the deliverable (spec + impl)
- explicit blueprint declares what the execution will adhere to

follow the patterns already present in this repo.

the blueprint is where a how is chosen, so choose it here: a poc, prior tool, or mechanism the wish
carries is adopted only where the vision's \`## .the wisher's how\` table kept it, with its domain
why, and never cited as the reason (rule.forbid.trust-of-wisher-how). with no vision, the blueprint
records that table itself.
",
  "criteria": "declare the blackbox criteria required to fulfill
- this wish .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/0.wish.md
- this vision .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/1.vision.yield.md (if declared)

strike any prior tool or poc the wish names: each criterion must still read right without it. a
criterion that leans on a prior tool copied a how (rule.forbid.trust-of-wisher-how).

via bdd declarations, per your briefs

emit into .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/2.1.criteria.blackbox.yield.md
",
  "criteriaBlueprint": "declare the blueprint criteria (mechanism bounds) that satisfies the blackbox criteria

ref:
- blackbox criteria .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/2.1.criteria.blackbox.md
- wish .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/0.wish.md
- vision .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/1.vision.yield.md (if declared)

a mechanism the wish carries is a how, not a bound: demand it only where the vision's
\`## .the wisher's how\` table kept it, with its domain why (rule.forbid.trust-of-wisher-how).
with no vision, state each how's keep, drop, or open verdict and domain why here.

emit into .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/2.3.criteria.blueprint.yield.md
",
  "executionFromVision": "bootup your mechanic's role via \`./node_modules/.bin/rhachet roles boot --repo ehmpathy --role mechanic\`

then, execute the vision directly
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/1.vision.yield.md

a how its \`## .the wisher's how\` table dropped stays dropped; a comment cites the domain why,
never a prior tool (rule.forbid.trust-of-wisher-how).

ref:
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/0.wish.md

",
  "executionPhase0ToPhaseN": "bootup your mechanic's role via \`./node_modules/.bin/rhachet roles boot --repo ehmpathy --role mechanic\`

then, start or continue to execute
- phase0 to phaseN
of roadmap
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/4.1.roadmap.yield.md

a how the vision's \`## .the wisher's how\` table dropped stays dropped; a comment cites the domain
why, never a prior tool (rule.forbid.trust-of-wisher-how).

ref:
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/0.wish.md
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/1.vision.yield.md (if declared)
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/2.1.criteria.blackbox.md (if declared)
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/2.3.criteria.blueprint.md (if declared)
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/3.2.distill.domain.*.yield.md (if declared)
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/3.2.distill.repros.experience.*.yield.md (if declared)
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/3.3.0.blueprint.factory.yield.md (if declared)
- $BEHAVIOR_DIR_REL/3.3.1.blueprint.product.yield.md

",
  "vision": "illustrate the vision implied in the wish .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/0.wish.md

trust the wish's why, and its contract roughly (verbs, rough shape). any how it carries is evidence,
never spec: restate each how in domain terms with a keep, drop, or open verdict, in the
\`## .the wisher's how\` section below (rule.forbid.trust-of-wisher-how).

emit into .behavior/v2025_01_01.test-feature/1.vision.yield.md
",
}
`;
